trait KindProofSeal {}
/// Whether a kind slot can hold a MISSING placeholder: the KIND AXIS of a
/// generated carrier's type.
///
/// A slot whose kind the compiled grammar can prove never MISSING (a visible,
/// named, unaliased nonterminal; see [`CompiledLanguage::nonmissing_kind`]) is
/// a NARROWED slot. Its `Missing` payload is [`NarrowedMissing<K, M>`], which
/// holds a `K::Missing<M>`, where `M` is the payload every other kind slot
/// carries, so one carrier definition describes both readings:
///
/// | | [`Broad`] | [`KindAdmitted`] |
/// |---|---|---|
/// | `Missing<M>` | `M` | [`Never`] |
/// | `Evidence` | `()` | [`CanonicalLanguage`] |
///
/// Only a carrier or choice that reaches a narrowed slot (directly, or through
/// a nested carrier or choice) declares a `K: KindProof = Broad` parameter; a
/// shape with none has no kind axis at all, because both readings would be the
/// same type. With `K` concrete every projection normalizes, so
/// [`NonMissingKindSlot`] IS a `NodeSlot` whose `Missing` state is
/// uninhabited.
///
/// The proof is a TYPE, not a flag. Extraction under `KindAdmitted` needs a
/// [`CanonicalLanguage`] (its `Evidence`), which only the generated admission
/// can construct, and admits the node's language with it before reading a
/// child. Sealed: `Broad` and `KindAdmitted` are the only proofs, and both are
/// uninhabited markers.
///
